        "mission_intent": "We need to develop an automated continuous monitoring assessment framework that covers all common, hybrid, and system-specific security controls across every organizational system by the end of this quarter, while simultaneously requiring that each control's monitoring frequency be individually calibrated based on the aggregate criticality of the systems inheriting that control, the trustworthiness of common control providers, and the overall organizational risk posture. The framework should align with our ISCM strategy and produce dashboards at the mission/business processes tier that reflect real-time assessment status for all controls. Common controls inherited by large numbers of systems should be flagged for more frequent assessment cycles than controls protecting single systems, and the tooling should automate base control monitoring wherever feasible to support increased frequency. I'd like the team to use best efforts to ensure the frequency determinations are \"optimally risk-informed\" across all tiers, and the final product should be ready for agency-wide deployment within the same quarter even though we haven't yet completed the inventory of common control inheritance relationships across our subsidiary components. Please coordinate with the ISSO community and provide a status briefing at next month's governance board.",
